# TriliumNext ETAPI configuration for the AI bridge.
#
# HOW TO GET A TOKEN:
#   1. Open TriliumNext (the desktop app; the bridge launcher starts it at
#      http://localhost:8080).
#   2. Open Options: click the menu / gear icon (top-left "hamburger" menu ->
#      Options), then choose the "ETAPI" tab.
#      (If ETAPI requests are rejected, also check Options -> "Advanced" or
#       Settings -> Security and make sure the API is enabled.)
#   3. Click "Create new ETAPI token", give it a name (e.g. "ai-cli"), and copy
#      the token string it shows you (it is shown only once).
#   4. Copy this file to ".trilium-env" in the workspace root
#      (~/Desktop/AI CLI WORK/.trilium-env), paste the token below, then run:
#          chmod 600 ~/Desktop/AI\ CLI\ WORK/.trilium-env
#
# The bridge reads the environment variable first, then this file.

TRILIUM_ETAPI_TOKEN=
TRILIUM_URL=http://localhost:8080
